<title>CANADA: CWB details primary elevator space, railcar unload.</title>
<headline>CWB details primary elevator space, railcar unload.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Wheat Board said Wednesday available space in primary elevators across the Prairies remained unchanged from last week at 20 percent.</p>
<p>Space in Manitoba tightened slightly to 17 percent vacant from 18 percent the week before. Saskatchewan also tightened to 18 percent from 19. Alberta space opened to 27 percent vacant from 25 percent.</p>
<p>Hopper car unloads in Vancouver reached 3,445, up from the 3,400 target while Prince Rupert unloads were 1,133, down from the 1,500 target. Thunder Bay reached 2,788, down from the 3,100 target and 101 cars were unloaded in Churchill.</p>
<p>Churchill's shipping season ended Oct 29.</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
</text>
